            %p
              (adapted from
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Some+title+containing+the+words+%22homotopy%22+and+%22symplectic%22%2C+e.g.+this+one"} Ševera 00
          %h2#references References
          %p Lecture notes:
          %ul
            %li
              Miquel Cueca, Antonio Maglio, Fabricio Valencia:
              %em Lecture notes on the symplectic geometry of graded manifolds and higher Lie groupoids
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.09448"}> arXiv:2510.09448
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            The notion originates somewhere in the school of
            = succeed "\u2018s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alan+Weinstein"} Alan Weinstein
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher categorial
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+geometry"} symplectic geometry
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi n
                  %mo ≤
                  %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \leq n \leq 3
            is
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitry+Roytenberg"}> Dmitry Roytenberg
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Courant algebroids, derived brackets and even symplectic supermanifolds
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/9910078"} arXiv:9910078
          %p A good writeup of this material is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitry+Roytenberg"}> Dmitry Roytenberg
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em On the structure of graded symplectic supermanifolds and Courant algebroids
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theodore+Voronov"} Theodore Voronov
              (ed.),
              = succeed "," do
                %em Quantization, Poisson Brackets and Beyond
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 315
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0203110"} arXiv:0203110
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/conm-315"} ISBN:978-0-8218-7905-4
          %p
            The idea for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            was then sketched, together with many other ideas about
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-infinity+algebroid"} L-infinity algebroid
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pavol+%C5%A0evera"}> Pavol Ševera
              ,
              %em Some title containing the words “homotopy” and “symplectic”, e.g. this one
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0105080"}> arXiv
              )
          %p
            What we call
            = succeed "-symplectic" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-manifold" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_n
          %p
            %strong Warning
            This article here uses the term “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            \-symplectic” in a related but not identical sense to the one used here:
          %ul
            %li
              M. de Leon, D. Martin de Diego, M. Salgado, S. Vilariño,
              %em K-symplectic formalism on Lie algebroids
              (
              %a{:href => "http://lanl.arxiv.org/abs/0905.4585"}> arXiv
              )
          %p
            A discussion of aspects of how
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multisymplectic+geometry"} multisymplectic geometry
            related to
            = succeed "-symplectic" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Rogers"}> Chris Rogers
                \:
                %em Courant algebroids from categorified symplectic geometry
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1001.0040"}> arXiv:1001.0040
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Rogers"}> Chris Rogers
                ,
                %em Higher symplectic geometry
                PhD thesis (2011) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1106.4068"}> arXiv:1106.4068
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            A discussion of symplectic Lie n-algebroids from an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-Lie+theory"} infinity-Lie theory
            perspective as discussed here:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Rogers"} Chris Rogers
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/AKSZ+Sigma-Models+in+Higher+Chern-Weil+Theory"} AKSZ Sigma-Models in Higher Chern-Weil Theory
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1108.4378"} arXiv:1108.4378
          %p
            On the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H-cohomology"} H-cohomology
            of graded symplectic forms:
          %ul
            %li#Severa05
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pavol+Severa"}> Pavol Severa
              , p. 1 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em On the origin of the BV operator on odd symplectic supermanifolds
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0506331"} arXiv:0506331
